26825,0.0,-0.0027938163839280605,-0.7481255531311035,-4.6491513785440475e-06,-4.768370445162873e-07,-0.4596790671348572,-0.016485197469592094,-0.014862054958939552,-1.2397689715726301e-05,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.06465356796979904,-0.002017606981098652,-1.1324817933200393e-05,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,-5.960462772236497e-07,-0.11770313233137131,-1.3251535892486572,0.0,0.0,-0.00026306029758416116,-2.622600959512056e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,1372,220,17,19,646,387,1865,553,84192,3786,3040,10250,5109,25,220,17,11,220,17,11,220,17,323,220,18,13,2585,1657,49433,1969,387,54916,311,1281,220,17,19,15,15,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe number 24 can be made by multiplying together four prime numbers: 2, 2, 2 and 3. How many primes must be multiplied to make 2400?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"fab1c4c52112c314f16203b0e2863edc4ef43958df7ddcc1f89bc7ef0e417d03"},"seconds":33.04265737533569,"seed":1022485419845042843,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we first need to factorize 2400 into its prime factors. Let's begin with the prime factorization of 2400 step by step.\n\n1. Start with the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n   - 2400 is even, so we can divide by 2.\n   \\[\n   2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n   \\]\n   - 1200 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   1200 \\div 2 = 600\n   \\]\n   - 600 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   600 \\div 2 = 300\n   \\]\n   - 300 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   300 \\div 2 = 150\n   \\]\n   - 150 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   150 \\div 2 = 75\n   \\]\n\n2. 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n   - 75 is divisible by 3.\n   \\[\n   75 \\div 3 = 25\n   \\]\n\n3. 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n   - 25 is divisible by 5.\n   \\[\n   25 \\div 5 = 5\n   \\]\n   - 5 is divisible by 5.\n   \\[\n   5 \\div 5 = 1\n   \\]\n\n4. Therefore, the prime factorization of 2400 is:\n   \\[\n   2400 = 2^5 \\times 3 \\times 5^2\n   \\]\n\n5. Now, we count the total number of prime factors:\n   - The prime factor 2 appears 5 times.\n   - The prime factor 3 appears 1 time.\n   - The prime factor 5 appears 2 times.\n\n6. Sum up the total number of prime factors:\n   \\[\n   5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of primes that must be multiplied to make 2400 is \\boxed{8}."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{8}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To solve this problem, we first need to factorize 2400 into its prime factors. Let's begin with the prime factorization of 2400 step by step.\n\n1. Start with the smallest prime number, which is 2.\n   - 2400 is even, so we can divide by 2.\n   \\[\n   2400 \\div 2 = 1200\n   \\]\n   - 1200 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   1200 \\div 2 = 600\n   \\]\n   - 600 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   600 \\div 2 = 300\n   \\]\n   - 300 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   300 \\div 2 = 150\n   \\]\n   - 150 is even, so we can divide by 2 again.\n   \\[\n   150 \\div 2 = 75\n   \\]\n\n2. 75 is not divisible by 2, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 3.\n   - 75 is divisible by 3.\n   \\[\n   75 \\div 3 = 25\n   \\]\n\n3. 25 is not divisible by 3, so we move to the next smallest prime number, which is 5.\n   - 25 is divisible by 5.\n   \\[\n   25 \\div 5 = 5\n   \\]\n   - 5 is divisible by 5.\n   \\[\n   5 \\div 5 = 1\n   \\]\n\n4. Therefore, the prime factorization of 2400 is:\n   \\[\n   2400 = 2^5 \\times 3 \\times 5^2\n   \\]\n\n5. Now, we count the total number of prime factors:\n   - The prime factor 2 appears 5 times.\n   - The prime factor 3 appears 1 time.\n   - The prime factor 5 appears 2 times.\n\n6. Sum up the total number of prime factors:\n   \\[\n   5 + 1 + 2 = 8\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total number of primes that must be multiplied to make 2400 is \\boxed{8}.","id":"prealgebra:753"}
